# Qwen3.6-35B-A3B MXFP4, 4 x MI455X, MLPerf Endpoints agentic: the 2026-11-23 settings, on top of agentic_20261101.env,
# agentic_20261107.env, agentic_20261119.env, agentic_20261120.env and agentic_20261121.env (README, 2026-11-23 section).
# Code: alizaidy/gfx1250-qwen-support plus the aiter one-shot split reduce shape rule (+ its ATOM fold hook) and the aiter
# 3D decode XCD rotation.

# One-shot split-KV reduce: (CHUNK, SPEC, warps) from the launch shape instead of the fixed 16,8,2 (bitwise; reduce
# 6.3 -> 3.1 us at 1 seq x 4 rows, -35..-48 us a decode step at 1-8 seqs; c64 +1.6%). Served-measured at c64-c512.
AITER_GFX12_SPLIT_REDUCE_ONESHOT_AUTO=1

# --- c256-c512 only (set by the point, after its fp4pt split extras) ---
# 3D decode: rotate the sequences by the segment so a sequence's segments spread over the 8 XCDs (bitwise), and 896
# token-split programs (NUMERICAL: another split, so another fp32 summation order; needs the rotation, which removes
# the one-XCD overflow at 768-896). Together: c256 +2.2%, c384 +2.6%, c512 +1.8%; c64 is slower with the rotation
# (+2-8% kernel time at 4-8 seqs) and c1024 flat.
#   AITER_UA3D_XCD_ROTATE=1 AITER_GFX12_TOKEN_SPLIT_PROGRAMS=896
